        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>In a blast furnace, iron is extracted from haematite ($Fe_2O_3$) by reducing it with carbon monoxide ($CO$), which is produced from the reaction of coke (carbon) with oxygen. The other options (hydrogen, nitrogen, and chlorine) are not used in this reduction process.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
